eywords":[{"value":"UNIFIED FIELD THEORY","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"GAUGE FIELD THEORY: ASYMPTOTIC FREEDOM","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"GAUGE FIELD THEORY: E6","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"GAUGE FIELD THEORY: HIERARCHY","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"INTERMEDIATE BOSON: MASS","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"MASS: INTERMEDIATE BOSON","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"MODEL: HIGGS","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"RENORMALIZATION GROUP: CALLAN-SYMANZIK EQUATION","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"APPROXIMATION: TREE","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"QUARK: LEPTONIC","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"QUARK: MASS","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"MASS: QUARK","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"LEPTON: MASS","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"MASS: LEPTON","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"FERMION: MULTIPLET","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"MULTIPLET: FERMION","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"NEUTRINO: MASS","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"MASS: NEUTRINO","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"POSTULATED PARTICLE: HEAVY LEPTON","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"NUMERICAL CALCULATIONS","schema":"INSPIRE"}],"refereed":true,"abstracts":[{"value":"The hierarchy of gauge interactions within the E 6 model is proved, and the vector and spinor field masses are obtained. The mass spectrum of the charged W-bosons is found, and the mass scale is fixed so that the mass of the lightest of them is about 70 GeV. The lepton spectroscopy is studied and a new charged lepton, with mass of order 4–8 GeV is predicted. For the low-energy phenomenology, the model may be considered as a theory of 6 flavoured quarks and 4 charged leptons, each with its neutrino. Being 4-component the neutrinos are massive except for the ν e ( m ν e = 0, exactly) and ν μ ( m ν μ ≈ 0, approximately) particles. The problem of the “superfluous” particles which as a rule accompanies the asymptotic freedom in such theories is also briefly discussed.","source":"Elsevier"}],"copyright":[{"statement":"Copyright @ unknown. Published by Elsevier B.V."}],"references":[{"reco